  "The five largest coordinates have ZERO occurrences in orgs/kotoba-lang:
   org.clojure/data.json 27, metosin/jsonista 21, http-kit/http-kit 19,
   ring/ring-core 12, metosin/reitit-ring 9 -- 88 declarations, none of them
   in scope. They are one shape (JSON codec + HTTP server + ring + routing)
   and they sit in one application family. Three of the five already have a
   :first-party-exists disposition below, so for those the substitute exists
   and the SCOPE is what excludes the repositories that would use it.
   Widening the scope is a decision this ledger's owner makes; naming the gap
   is not."

  :the-coverage-gap
  "Six coordinates carry no entry at all -- 36 declarations. Candidate targets
   below were found with `nbb scripts/repo-search.cljs` and read out of each
   repository's README; they are CANDIDATES, not dispositions, and are
   recorded that way deliberately. A disposition asserts that a substitution
   is the right move, which is a judgement; this is only the measurement that
   a plausible first-party target exists and can be checked in one command."
